{
  "summary": "Enables clang-tidy's `readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name` check and updates mismatched parameter names across declarations and definitions throughout the codebase. It also removes unused serialization overloads for `unique_ptr<const T>` and marks functions used only within their own translation units as static.",
  "problem": "Parameter names between function declarations in headers and definitions in source files drift apart over time, causing inconsistency and slight confusion during development.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Declarations and definitions tend to drift apart. We could align these, and then enforce that via clang-tidy... This may not be worth the (initial) churn / we may also be fine with inconsistency here.'"
  ],
