    "depends_on": [
      "#36743"
    ],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "A wide-ranging mechanical refactor touching 75 files to rename parameters in declarations or definitions, combined with clang-tidy configuration updates. It is based on #36743 to avoid double-churn on functions being removed or made static.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Enforces consistent parameter naming between function declarations and definitions across the codebase by enabling clang-tidy's readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name check. Parameter names in headers and implementations drift apart over time, reducing code clarity. The author opened this as an RFC, noting that the community must decide whether the initial churn across 75 files is worth the consistency benefit. Based on #36743.",
